    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a structured address form (`addressLine1` + optional `addressLine2`) alongside the existing flat `address`, preferring the structured fields when present while staying backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they're accepted on requests and returned on `Owner` responses).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list \u2014 otherwise a structured-only request (no flat `address`) would be rejected by generated `@NotNull` validation before reaching the controller. `city` stays required.\n- Documented `address` on the response as the composed, normalized value.\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns + getters/setters; dropped the now-invalid `@NotEmpty` on `address` (it's always set to the composed value).\n\n**Schema DDL** \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb is what the tests use; ddl-auto is `none`). Also relaxed h2's `address NOT NULL` since address can now derive from the structured form.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- New `applyAddress(...)`: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`address` with the existing `normalizeAddress` rules; when a non-blank `addressLine1` is present the structured form wins, otherwise it falls back to flat `address`. It stores normalized line1/line2 and sets `address` to the composed string (`line1` + a single space + `line2` when line2 is present).\n- `validateRequiredFields`: the `address` error now fires only when **both** `addressLine1` and flat `address` are blank, so minimal legacy owners and new structured owners both validate.\n\nMapStruct maps the two new fields automatically by name in both directions.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 structured normalization/composition and continued flat-address acceptance \u2014 both pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
